 This is a diagnostic path only; it does not relax any downstream freshness gates.
+
+### Reflective native profiles and diagnostic exports
+
+`CalibrationCamera.native_laser_snapshot(max_age_s=1., not_before_monotonic=None)`
+returns one existing cached native exposure as lossless `frame_png_base64`, image
+hashes/size/channel order, exact source/generation/session/calibration/timing and
+sensor controls, plus that observation's own `cloud` and measurement settings.
+The image is unscaled, unannotated and has no preview tone mapping. A newer
+independently published cloud is never substituted. This diagnostic opens no
+camera, changes no controls, writes no files and makes no stationary robot/world
+registration claim. A failed/no-return detection can still export its real image
+with `cloud=None` and `cloud_error`. Stale, changed-identity or pre-cutoff images
+are rejected.
+
+Reflective laser preparation may opt into `AutoExposure(gain_enabled=True,
+min_gain_db=0., max_gain_db=18., gain_step_db=3.)`. Existing exposure-only behavior
+is unchanged by default. `ExposureController.update_controls(...)` and the
+pipeline prefer exposure time before gain within configured sensor/FPS bounds;
+they replace amplification with exposure when possible, reduce inherited or
+clipping gain, and raise gain only for a coherent unsaturated dim stripe at its
+exposure cap. Gain cannot brighten an ambiguous view blindly. Every proposal is
+bound to the measured frame, configuration, generation and actual controls; only
+the existing acquisition owner applies it, invalidates old results and drains
+buffered images before further feedback. A nominal 20-log gain approximation is
+an initial exposure proposal, never optical calibration or qualification.
+
+`Detection.min_snr` defaults to zero. When positive, each candidate must exceed
+both the configured contrast floor and `min_snr` times a robust raw scanline
+shoulder-noise estimate (neighbor-difference MAD, with a 1-DN floor). Accepted
+centroids remain the original native measurements. Metadata records measured
+noise rejection diagnostics. This allows a small contrast floor on a faint
+surface without accepting equally small high-gain noise peaks. Multiple returns
+on one scanline and native clipping remain independent measurement rejections.
+
+`PointCloudNoise.min_run_points` defaults to zero. A positive value rejects short
+native runs remaining after the local-neighbor pass, including orphan points
+whose original neighbors were themselves rejected. Every sufficiently long run
+is retained; the longest component is not presumed to be the desired surface.
+No smoothing or interpolation bridges real discontinuities or missing returns.
+A coherent secondary reflection can still survive these camera-only rules and
+requires independent feature/model association.
+
+`SeamSettings.feature_kinds` explicitly limits the supported feature types to a
+nonempty subset of `valley`, `step`, and `inside_corner`; the default includes
+all three for compatibility. Filtering occurs before feature selection and
+ambiguity resolution. Excluding a feature does not make a native gap proof of a
+physical seam endpoint. Sensor settings or image filtering never rescale the
+installed optical/laser calibration or fabricate a measured weld root.
+
+When an explicit non-full `Detection.roi` selects the seam measurement, the
+pipeline retains `cloud.full_profile` as full-frame camera-mm display context
+from the exact same native frame, calibration, controls, timing and noise/depth
+settings. It has role `full_native_profile_context`, `not_seam_measurement=True`
+and the explicit normalized `measurement_roi`; no nested context is created.
+This preserves complete red native profile spans without treating context as a
+second seam measurement. Full-frame requests retain their single extraction pass.
+
+`project_camera_points(points_mm, calibration, source_id, image_size)` projects
+finite positive-depth camera-frame points through a matching installed optical
+model and returns native `uv`, `inside_image`, canonical `calibration_id` and
+`optical_intrinsics_id`. Out-of-sensor pixels stay outside without clipping. This
+is explicitly a prediction for choosing a sensing ROI, never a measured return.
+The robot owner must bind calibration/hand-eye identities and actual camera poses.
